watch dogs too has been on my radar  since was announced this summer and  after sitting down with it for a couple  hours i'm happy to say that it's shaping  up to be the sequel we hope for this  time around you play as Marcus Holloway  a talented young hacker who grew up in  Oakland just east of San Francisco from  what I played players will be spending  most of their time in San Francisco but  the map extends from Marin up north all  the way down to Silicon Valley in the  demo we were asked to stay within San  Francisco but there was still plenty to  do and see the map isn't an exact  recreation of San Francisco but many of  the famous landmarks like Golden Gate  Bridge and the palace of the Fine Arts  have been meticulously recreated  but watch Docs to has more to offer than  a new setting for starters the hacking  is more robust while hacking in the  original game felt limited in contextual  watchdogs to gives the player a bevy of  options when you targeted NPC a hacking  menu appears and from there you can hack  it to the bank account you can set off  their phone to cause a distraction and  you can even have the cops arrest them  but phones aren't the only things you  can manipulate Marcus can also hack and  control cars or even set traps these  might seem like small features but being  able to use them to cause mayhem from  afar was incredibly rewarding  the improved hacking options also  translate well into the mission  structure open-ended missions are  nothing new but all the new hacking  abilities available to add another layer  of depth in one mission I had to break  into a fortified dock steal the truck  and drive it back to a dead sec base  getting to the truck was easy but  finding the code to the gate was locked  behind was another story I could have  gone my way through goons until I found  the guard with the code but I decided to  take a more stealthy approach using my  drone I surveyed the area until I found  a guard I could hack the digital keys  from and voila unfortunately my luck ran  out as I was trying to leave the dock a  guard spotted me in the chase hit the  streets fortunately the driving is  noticeably better and watchdogs to as  control is much more responsive maybe a  bit too responsible times but it's a  necessary change that lends itself to  the tight and narrow streets of San  Francisco in another mission I was  tasked with breaking into a heavily  secured mansion and once again I let my  robotic companions do most of the  legwork I only played a few missions  during my time of the game but watch  dogs too appears to embrace a level of  freedom not seen in the first that  encourages both creativity and  experimentation  you  911 please state your emergency  watch dogs two-story also feels like a  departure from the first Marcus Holloway  is a refreshing protagonist compared to  Aiden Pearce he is much more  lighthearted than the tone seems to  follow suit rather than being a lone  wolf type Marcus has a group of fellow  hackers he's constantly keeping in touch  with and working alongside wildly  supporting characters still need time to  grow on me hearing Marcus quit with them  is a welcome change compared to Aiden's  constant humorless brooding you've got a  weird relationship with technology you  know that right like Assassin's Creed  from last generation watchdogs to seems  to improve upon the first in nearly  every way with the quality of its  vibrant setting and expanded hacking  options it feels like watch dogs 2's on  the right path but we won't know for  sure until the game launches on November  15 for more on watch dogs to subscribe  to our YouTube channel and head on over  to gamespot com  you
 

